    docs: fix CONTRIBUTING setup, test counts, and lint guidance. Addresses DOC-2.
    
    - Replace the dead `pip install -e ".[dev]"` setup with the repo workflow
      `uv sync --dev`: [dev] is a PEP 735 dependency group in pyproject.toml,
      not a pip extras section, so the old command fails on a fresh clone.
      A runnable pip fallback (`python3 -m pip install -e . pytest "ruff==0.16.8"`)
      is documented for hosts without uv.
    - Drop the dead coverage example: pytest-cov is not in the dev group and
      `--cov` fails with "unrecognized arguments" in the uv-managed .venv.
    - Correct per-file counts to fresh pytest --collect-only evidence
      (2026-09-27, repo .venv): test_plugin 16 (was 31+1 skipped),
      test_install 66 (was 11), test_standalone_cli 21 (was 15),
      test_metrics_export 21 (unchanged).
    - Replace the phantom plugin/test_integration.py tree entry with the real
      integration-bearing layout: @pytest.mark.integration lives in
      test_env_scrub, test_userns, test_backend_parity, test_backend_selection,
      and test_host_probes (no invented replacement count).
    - Line-length guidance 100 -> 88 to match pyproject.toml
      ([tool.ruff] line-length).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
